feat 1.0

# SPEC-ADPKUR-002 — Kurrent adapter: transport faults on the system's path. Agreed by founder ruling 58a4ac88 ("flip them, queue in that order"); rulings c7af7871 applied. Integration tier only:
# this file is excluded from the spec tier (specs.exclude: **/transport.feat) because the
# in-process spec host has no wire to cut. The mechanism is SPEC-FPX-001; this spec states what
# the product adapter promises on top of it.
#
# Topology: the system's KurrentDB client (gRPC over HTTP/2) is pointed at the proxy's listen address; the adapter's instrument client at the product directly (connectionString vs proxy.upstream). TLS: the product's certificate must name the proxy host or the system's client must run with tlsVerifyCert=false (insecure single node in the test fixture, DESIGN.md).
# BrokerLoss is not here: it is exclusive and lives in broker-loss.feat (serial pass, SPEC-RT-005).
# Fixture: a KurrentDB container the TEST starts and a Toxiproxy container in front of it.
# `ObserveKurrentTransport { script }` runs a space-separated script against the adapter of SPEC-ADPKUR-001
# with `options.proxy` set. Steps: `setup:<ns>`, `start:<ns>`, `stop:<ns>`, `settle:<ns>`,
# `reset:<ns>`, `fired:<ns>`, `fault:<ns>:Connection.<Fault>[:once]`, and `write:<ns>:...`
# (the SYSTEM writes through the proxy); a Connection fault has no stream or topic segment, only an optional count. UNAVAILABLE, DEADLINE_EXCEEDED and CANCELLED from the client are all reported as TRANSPORT_FAILURE. Trace and counts as in SPEC-ADPKUR-001.
#
# What the scenarios decide: a transport fault is on the SYSTEM's path only; the adapter observes
# on its own direct connection, so under a fault the capture, the fence and the state read still
# work, and an absence under a fault is still provable. Whether the fault was consumed is
# unobserved (the proxy reports bytes, not activations: DESIGN.md of the fault-proxy library).

spec SPEC-ADPKUR-002 "Kurrent adapter: transport faults on the system's path"
context Toolchain
aggregate Adapters
type infrastructure
status agreed

construct:
  handler at adapters/kurrent/src/index.ts
  touches adapters/kurrent/**
  needs SPEC-FPX-001
  needs SPEC-ADPKUR-001
  Add `Connection: { Timeout: ["reset"], ConnectionReset: ["reset"], Partition: ["reset"] }` to the fault catalog when `options.proxy` is configured
  (`{ api, name }` plus, for container control, `container`); without it the catalog has no
  Connection entry. fault() with Connection delegates to the shared fault-proxy library; reset()
  calls the library's disarm. The adapter's own clients never use the proxy.

enforce:
  rejects FAULT_UNSUPPORTED when a Connection fault is armed with a count it does not declare (only until reset), or without options.proxy
  the adapter's observation is on a connection the proxy does not carry
  reset removes every toxic, re-enables the proxy and restores a stopped or paused container

contract:
  input ObserveInput
  response ObserveResult
  error ObserveError

scenario "a partition on the system's path refuses its write and leaves the observation intact":
  when: ObserveKurrentTransport { script: "setup:a start:a fault:a:Connection.Partition write:a:orders:Placed settle:a stop:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a start:a fault:a:Connection.Partition write:a!TRANSPORT_FAILURE settle:a=true stop:a=0" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "a connection reset on the system's path refuses its write the same way":
  when: ObserveKurrentTransport { script: "setup:a start:a fault:a:Connection.ConnectionReset write:a:orders:Placed settle:a stop:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a start:a fault:a:Connection.ConnectionReset write:a!TRANSPORT_FAILURE settle:a=true stop:a=0" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "a timeout on the system's path surfaces as a transport failure after the client's deadline":
  when: ObserveKurrentTransport { script: "setup:a start:a fault:a:Connection.Timeout write:a:orders:Placed settle:a stop:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a start:a fault:a:Connection.Timeout write:a!TRANSPORT_FAILURE settle:a=true stop:a=0" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "reset heals the path, so the same write is then captured":
  when: ObserveKurrentTransport { script: "setup:a fault:a:Connection.Partition reset:a start:a write:a:orders:Placed settle:a stop:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a fault:a:Connection.Partition reset:a start:a write:a settle:a=true stop:a=1", last: "orders/Placed" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "the proxy reports no activation, so firedFaults is not offered":
  when: ObserveKurrentTransport { script: "setup:a fault:a:Connection.Partition fired:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a fault:a:Connection.Partition fired:a=unobserved" }
    filesystem has []

scenario outline "a transport fault that the proxy cannot scope to one call is refused":
  when: ObserveKurrentTransport { script: <script> }
  predict rejection FAULT_UNSUPPORTED:
    response ERR ObserveError { code: "FAULT_UNSUPPORTED", detail: matching <detail> }
    filesystem has []
  examples:
    | script                                        | detail |
    | "setup:a fault:a:Connection.Timeout:once"     | "once" |
    | "setup:a fault:a:Connection.Partition:times2" | "times" |
